{
  "_about": "Water and use profiles. Each scores a design 0-100. targets give [poor, good] for a metric; the score rises linearly between them, and past poor it keeps falling (to minus one full weight). weights say how much each metric counts. constraints are hard limits; a design that breaks one is marked and penalised. load sets crew posture (kneeling, low_seat, seated), weights and centre of gravity heights; see stability.load_case. waves are a JONSWAP sea: significant height (m), peak period (s), gamma (1 developed swell, 3.3 wind chop, 5-7 short steep waves). depth_m is water depth, null for deep.",
